'" Robotics kinematics example `robotics_kinematics.cpp`
@startuml robotics_kinematics
title Robotics kinematics: planar arm FK/IK and Jacobian flow
actor User as Main
participant "Example (robotics_kinematics)" as Example
participant "PlanarRobotArm" as Arm
participant "Mat<float, 2, 2>" as Jacobian

Main -> Example: run()
Example -> Arm: forward_kinematics(theta1, theta2)
Arm -> Example: end effector position
Example -> Arm: inverse_kinematics(target, elbow_up)
Arm -> Example: joint angles
Example -> Arm: jacobian(theta1, theta2)
Arm -> Jacobian: build velocity map
Example -> Main: print FK, IK, and velocity results

note right
  The maintained example is a 2-link planar robot arm.
  It demonstrates closed-form IK plus the Jacobian
  for end-effector velocity mapping.
end note
@enduml
